🌱 Home Soil Moisture Detection System | Arduino Project

I’m excited to share my Soil Moisture Detection System, a simple home-based electronics project designed to monitor the moisture level of soil and help us understand when a plant may need watering.

🪴 Why I built this project

Plants at home need the right amount of water. Overwatering can be harmful, while underwatering can cause plants to dry out. This project demonstrates how a simple sensor and microcontroller can be used to monitor soil moisture and provide an indication of the soil condition.

⚙️ How it works

The system uses a soil moisture sensor placed inside the plant’s soil. The sensor detects changes associated with the moisture condition and sends a signal to the Arduino.

Arduino reads the sensor signal and processes it according to the programmed condition or threshold. The result can then be indicated using an LED or other output device.

